n the fifth lap, and winning by almost 10 seconds in a new world best time. His time was recorded as 9:21 4/5, but this was the first race in Olympic history where an electronic time was taken (a system was used at " [:a {:href "/editions/6/sports/ATH"} "Stockholm in 1912"] ", but no times have been found), and is known to us that time was 9:21.60."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "790"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67692"} "Toivo Loukola"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "9:37.6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "9:21.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "797"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "9:58.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "9:31.2 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "769"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67542"} "Ove Andersen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "– (2 h3)"] [:td {} "9:35.6 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "844"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/76118"} "Nils Eklöf"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/coun